-- W67 (O12, M14): an `if … else if …` ladder of 400 arms, twice the length that
-- exceeded the host parser's nesting (188). Each arm is the else branch
-- of the one before it; the ladder is cut into bindings that float out of
-- the branches — an arm whose conditions are provably total is evaluated
-- where the binding sits, one whose conditions are calls is a thunk
-- forced only when the arms before it fell through — and the arms are
-- tried in order, so a later `error` condition is never reached, exactly
-- as GHC. Pinned against GHC: the first, middle and last arms, the
-- fall-through, ladders of total and of called conditions, and a ladder
-- whose arms are in the then branch.

